  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling-up of high impact interventions in the fight against HIV/AIDS - Tajikistan (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tajikistan, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Tajikistan)This program has the following goals: To achieve universal access to HIV services; prevention, care, treatment and support that enables people with HIV to live a fulfilling life. The objectives of this program are: Ensure high quality and coverage of prevention services for key populations (PWID, SW, MSM, prisoners, including their partners).  Ensure quality care and treatment for the people living with HIV/AIDS and TB.  Health System Strengthening by integration of health service delivery and optimisation of human resources.  Programme management: capacity development of MoHSPP and support of procurement and supply management.  Strengthened supportive environment to improve access to services for Key Population</narrative>
  </description>
